<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bremen-Verden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1648">1648</a>–<a href="/years/1823">1823</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Duchy of Bremen-Verden, Duchies of Bremen and Verden</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bremen-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verden">Verden</a> was the territory formed from the secularised prince-archbishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a> and prince-bishopric of Verden, granted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> in 1648. Sweden claimed the city of Bremen as part of it and attacked it in 1654 and 1666. Occupied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>, it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a> in 1715–1719.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bremen-verden.jpg" alt="Bremen-Verden" width="320" height="271" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lower_Saxony_Landschaft_der_Herzogt%C3%BCmer_Bremen_und_Verden.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
